From 41fec2888ca399e22da3de65314b232c915fefe1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr233 <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:41:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 81/81] vgpu: read a condemned display surface's resident from
 compute

Component: compute staging, sampled type-11 surfaces.

When the wire guard condemns a surface's guest pages, they belong to
another surface, and the draw rail binds the surface's resident instead
(condemned_sampled_source). Compute staging still read the pages and
failed. macOS 27 captures each Liquid Glass backdrop with a kernel
sampling the display surface being composed, so in a boot where a
display surface was condemned every capture failed and its dispatch was
dropped.

A sampled type-11 window whose pages are condemned is now read from the
surface's resident when that is a ready device allocation, as on the
draw rail.

Measured on arm64 Linux (NVIDIA GB10), macOS 27.2 guest at protocol 237:
in a boot where mapping 2 was condemned, before, 27 failed reads of it,
each a dropped dispatch; after, in a boot where it was condemned again,
13 resident reads and no failure.

Verified: the reims-vgpu test suite passes; clippy unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
